 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "My Samsung dishwasher DW60M6050FS keeps showing 4C and beeping, won't do anything"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "The '4C' code on your Samsung dishwasher indicates a water supply issue—specifically that little to no fresh water is entering the machine. This usually happens because the tap isn't fully open, the inlet hose is kinked or blocked, or there's an issue with the inlet valve filter. To narrow this down, please check two things:\n1) Is the tap behind or under the dishwasher fully turned on?\n2) Look at the flexible water inlet hose at the back of the machine—is it kinked, crushed, or blocked? Let me know what you find."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Checked the hose, no kinks anywhere. Water pressure at the kitchen tap is fine too. There's a screwdriver-slot valve under the sink for the dishwasher, it's at 90 degrees to the pipe. Is that meant to be like that? A plumber fitted a new kitchen tap yesterday."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That orientation means the valve is closed. On these quarter-turn valves, the handle must be parallel to the pipe for water to flow. Since you had new taps fitted yesterday, it's likely this isolation valve was left off or bumped shut. Please turn that valve so the slot lines up with the pipe (parallel), then try starting a programme again. If it still shows 4C after opening the valve, we'll need to check for debris in the inlet filter at the back of the machine."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Turned the valve so it's parallel to the pipe and started a programme. It's filling and running normally now, thanks!"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That’s excellent news. Since the plumber fitted a new tap yesterday, it was very likely that the isolation valve was left in the closed position or bumped by accident. Just keep an eye on it to ensure the handle stays parallel to the pipe so water can flow freely next time you run it. If you need any more help with your dishwasher, just let me know."
  }
 ],
